    help_step1: "Select the root game folder (where the .exe file is located).",
    help_step2: "In settings (gear icon) choose the source and target language, then click <b>Extract Text</b> — the app unpacks RPA archives and collects all the game's text into a database. Each source → target pair is a separate workspace; you can keep several and switch between them in the <b>Translations</b> bar.",
    help_step3: "Open a file from the list and translate the lines. For batch work there's the <b>Assistant</b> (local LLM or copy-paste). Press <b>Save</b>.",
    help_step4: "Click <b>Build Mod</b> — the app generates the translation and injects the patch. Next to it: the font icon <b>T</b> for font replacement; the <b>&lt;/&gt;</b> button for expert delivery hooks (for non-standard statements our channels don't catch).",
    help_step5: "Launch the game — the translation applies instantly. If the game is already running, press <b>Shift+R</b> in its window to reload text without restarting. Game got an update? The <b>Update</b> button carries your translation over to the new version.",
    help_step6: "After a build, the translation can be exported for distribution: in the <b>Translations</b> bar, on a built pair click <b>Export</b> and choose <b>Full game</b> (a game copy with the translation included) or <b>Translation only</b> (files for game/ of the matching version).",
    help_step7: "Something didn't get extracted? The file panel has <b>Manual strings</b> — type text you see in the game but isn't in the list; it's delivered directly by text match.",
    help_note_langselect: "<b>Note:</b> the new translation overrides the language it was made from. If the game has a localization selector and you pick that source language in it, the game will show your translation, not the original. Tip: to avoid confusion, rename the selector button, e.g. «English» → «Русский».",
